1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:08,775
On-page SEO is arranging your shop window, so people and Google's robots understand at once what you sell.

2
00:00:09,480 --> 00:00:18,730
The title tag is the blue headline in search results. Put the main keyword near the start, and keep it under sixty characters.

3
00:00:19,420 --> 00:00:27,770
The meta description is the grey text underneath. It does not raise rankings, but a good one makes more people click.

4
00:00:29,480 --> 00:00:38,130
Before: the title just says Home, there are two big headings, an image with no description, and a link that says click here.

5
00:00:38,830 --> 00:00:48,655
After: a specific title with the city, one clear heading, sections underneath, every image described, and links that say where they go.

6
00:00:49,350 --> 00:00:55,500
Same business, same products. Now both people and Google understand the page.

7
00:00:57,210 --> 00:01:03,710
Use one main heading, then smaller headings for sections, like chapters in a textbook.

8
00:01:04,410 --> 00:01:13,135
Google cannot see pictures, so describe every image with alt text. And never write click here: say where the link goes.

9
00:01:13,830 --> 00:01:17,955
Write for people first. Now optimise the page.

